## Item 4 — not done, and why

Investigating the deferred `:ws/accept` frame send (`ws.cljc` accept-slot!) and disclaim branch, I found the client's `WsHandle` only leaves `:connecting` phase (unblocking `append!`, which answers `:dao.stream/full` until then) when `deliver!` receives that exact frame. Simply deleting the send would permanently strand every client in `:connecting`. The architecturally consistent fix — matching the server side, which already sets `:open` synchronously with no round trip — is to make the client do the same. But `connect!`'s contract explicitly promises not to wait for the peer, and at least one host (JS `WebSocket.send()` before its own `open` event throws) may not tolerate writes issued that early. Resolving this needs deliberate, cross-host-tested work I did not have room to do safely alongside the ruling's actual subject (items 1–3), and no test in the existing suite currently exercises it, so nothing regressed by leaving it alone — but per the brief it was one of five ordered work items, so I'm not marking it done.

Status: BLOCKED - item 4 (dao.stream.ws.cljc accept-frame/disclaim retirement) needs a coordinated client+server phase-transition redesign to avoid stranding every client in :connecting; items 1, 2, 3, and 5 are complete and verified per above.
